    "question_ar": "صمم شبكة AWS آمنة لتطبيقات المقر ووصول البعثات.",
    "answer_en": "I would place application and database tiers in private subnets across at least two availability zones, expose only the required entry points through controlled load balancers or API gateways, and use security groups as the main workload firewall. Administrative access should use Systems Manager or a tightly controlled management path, not open SSH or RDP. HQ and missions can connect through site-to-site VPN, with Transit Gateway where scale justifies it, VPC endpoints for private AWS-service access, central DNS and logging, and a continuity plan for missions when the WAN is unavailable.",
