    "question_en": "How would you design backup and disaster recovery in AWS across regions and accounts?",
    "question_ar": "كيف ستصمم النسخ الاحتياطي والتعافي في AWS عبر المناطق والحسابات؟",
    "answer_en": "I would begin with business-approved RTO and RPO for each service. AWS Backup policies would create encrypted, immutable copies with cross-account protection and cross-region replication where the risk case justifies it. Databases may use Multi-AZ for availability and separate cross-region recovery mechanisms; S3 may use versioning and replication; and infrastructure should be reproducible through code. The decisive control is not the presence of backups but successful scheduled restore and failover tests, documented runbooks, named owners and reconciliation of recovered data.",
